From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 23:18:04 -0400
Subject: archive: unpinned tabs idle past a threshold leave the sidebar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Auto-archive, as Arc does it: a per-window TabArchiver sweeps every five
minutes and closes unpinned tabs outside folders that nobody has looked at
for longer than stedding.archive.idle_hours (12 by default, 0 = off), into
the recently-closed list so Shift-Cmd-T brings one back. Pinned tabs in
either tier, folder tabs and the active tab are never touched. The idle
clock is the archiver's own (opened or activated as it saw it), so a tab
opened in the background counts from when it appeared. A dropdown in the
Stedding settings section sets the threshold.

Why: PRODUCT.md, "Unpinned Tabs — auto-archived when idle"; the sidebar
stays a working set instead of a graveyard. docs/features/archive.md A1-A6.

Removable when: never; this is product behaviour.
